WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.979
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:08.677
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.977 --> 00:00:18.119
Unit sixteen: C1 Advanced: Overview and Use of English. Today you will understand C1 Advanced and handle advanced cloze and word formation.

4
00:00:18.419 --> 00:00:21.245
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.549
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.383 --> 00:00:27.396
Advanced.

7
00:00:28.383 --> 00:00:30.394
Advanced means at a high level.

8
00:00:30.983 --> 00:00:34.144
C1 Advanced is a high-level exam.

9
00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.379
Your turn. Say: Advanced.

10
00:00:40.233 --> 00:00:41.223
Advanced.

11
00:00:41.983 --> 00:00:42.880
Nuance.

12
00:00:43.883 --> 00:00:46.138
Nuance means a small difference in meaning.

13
00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.134
Notice the nuance.

14
00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:51.402
Your turn. Say: Nuance.

15
00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:55.314
Nuance.

16
00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:57.098
Collocation.

17
00:00:58.083 --> 00:01:00.698
Collocation means words that often go together.

18
00:01:01.283 --> 00:01:03.074
A strong collocation.

19
00:01:03.683 --> 00:01:06.278
Your turn. Say: Collocation.

20
00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:10.320
Collocation.

21
00:01:11.083 --> 00:01:11.945
Idiom.

22
00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:15.635
Idiom means a fixed phrase with a special meaning.

23
00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:17.936
Break the ice is an idiom.

24
00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.784
Your turn. Say: Idiom.

25
00:01:23.633 --> 00:01:24.460
Idiom.

26
00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:26.206
Cohesion.

27
00:01:27.217 --> 00:01:29.448
Cohesion means the way ideas connect.

28
00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:31.933
The text has strong cohesion.

29
00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:34.761
Your turn. Say: Cohesion.

30
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:38.659
Cohesion.

31
00:01:39.417 --> 00:01:40.743
Sophisticated.

32
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:44.179
Sophisticated means complex and refined.

33
00:01:44.783 --> 00:01:47.027
Use sophisticated vocabulary.

34
00:01:47.617 --> 00:01:50.339
Your turn. Say: Sophisticated.

35
00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.584
Sophisticated.

36
00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:56.258
Precision.

37
00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.122
Precision means exactness.

38
00:01:59.717 --> 00:02:01.124
Precision matters.

39
00:02:01.717 --> 00:02:04.415
Your turn. Say: Precision.

40
00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:08.128
Precision.

41
00:02:08.883 --> 00:02:10.093
Transformation.

42
00:02:11.083 --> 00:02:14.499
Transformation means a rewritten sentence with the same meaning.

43
00:02:15.083 --> 00:02:16.572
Do the transformation.

44
00:02:17.183 --> 00:02:19.731
Your turn. Say: Transformation.

45
00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:23.962
Transformation.

46
00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:28.476
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:29.317 --> 00:02:31.456
Visal, what is C1 Advanced?

48
00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:45.535
C1 Advanced is a Cambridge exam at an advanced level. It shows that you can use English fluently for study and work, and it is accepted by many universities and employers.

49
00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.568
What does Use of English test?

50
00:02:49.683 --> 00:03:05.327
It tests vocabulary, grammar and word formation at a high level. In the multiple-choice cloze you choose the word with the exact nuance and collocation, and in the open cloze you supply a grammar word.

51
00:03:06.417 --> 00:03:07.754
How do I prepare?

52
00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:23.542
Read widely, notice collocations and idioms, and keep a notebook of word families. For key word transformations, practise advanced structures such as inversion and cleft sentences.

53
00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.374
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:27.217 --> 00:03:31.712
Grammar focus: Strategy: nuance, collocation, accuracy.

55
00:03:32.012 --> 00:03:33.234
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:37.331
Not only did she win the prize, but she also broke the record.

57
00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:41.168
The word 'deeply' collocates with concerned, not with big.

58
00:03:42.133 --> 00:03:49.383
At C1 small differences in meaning and collocation decide the answer. Read widely and practise advanced structures such as inversion.

59
00:03:50.117 --> 00:03:54.058
Be careful! Don't say: I ignore the nuance of a word.

60
00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.801
Say: I check nuance and collocation.

61
00:03:59.101 --> 00:04:00.531
Nuance matters.

62
00:04:01.333 --> 00:04:03.835
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:04:04.633 --> 00:04:06.041
Advanced Practice.

64
00:04:06.341 --> 00:04:08.689
Mony studies for C1 Advanced.

65
00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:12.443
He notices that deeply collocates with concerned.

66
00:04:13.433 --> 00:04:16.977
He writes the phrase in his notebook with a note about its register.

67
00:04:17.967 --> 00:04:21.000
In a transformation he uses inversion with Not only.

68
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.220
His accuracy improves each week.

69
00:04:25.333 --> 00:04:29.265
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:30.117 --> 00:04:32.302
C1 Advanced is a blank exam.

71
00:04:32.602 --> 00:04:36.348
A, only speaking. B, high-level. C, beginner.

72
00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.050
The answer is B: high-level.

73
00:04:43.217 --> 00:04:45.193
Which collocation is natural?

74
00:04:45.493 --> 00:04:49.797
A, big concerned. B, deeply tall. C, deeply concerned.

75
00:04:53.333 --> 00:04:55.600
The answer is C: deeply concerned.

76
00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:59.667
'Not only did she win' is an example of blank.

77
00:04:59.967 --> 00:05:03.829
A, inversion. B, a question. C, a number.

78
00:05:07.367 --> 00:05:09.053
The answer is A: inversion.

79
00:05:10.217 --> 00:05:12.820
Use of English tests vocabulary and blank.

80
00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:17.075
A, only music. B, grammar. C, only maths.

81
00:05:20.633 --> 00:05:22.656
The answer is B: grammar.

82
00:05:23.817 --> 00:05:25.236
What does Mony keep?

83
00:05:25.536 --> 00:05:29.654
A, a map. B, a diary of food. C, a notebook.

84
00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.757
The answer is C: a notebook.

85
00:05:36.967 --> 00:05:40.095
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:43.669
How do you prepare for Use of English at C1?

87
00:05:52.483 --> 00:05:53.972
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:54.272 --> 00:06:09.431
I read widely and write down collocations and idioms. I practise advanced structures such as inversion and cleft sentences. I do timed tasks and review every mistake to improve my accuracy.

89
00:06:09.731 --> 00:06:11.661
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:18.488
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: nuance, collocation, accuracy.

91
00:06:18.788 --> 00:06:23.124
Today's value is lifelong learning. Keep learning for as long as you live.

92
00:06:23.424 --> 00:06:26.250
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:29.319
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

